w creation of custom upscalers. It's based on the same approach we've used for compositor effects, e.g once configured the rendering engine does a callback into the custom code to perform the actual upscaling.\r\n\r\nThe current approach only targets Forward+ and performs upscaling right after 3D rendering but before post processing similar to FSR2 and Temporal MetalFX. In theory you should be able to re-implement either using this approach.\r\n\r\nVery simple test project that does a 2x2 upscale:\r\nhttps://codeberg.org/BastiaanOlij/test-custom-upscaler\r\n\r\nOnly outstanding issue that I'm not sure how to solve is that I can't set project settings for this so the default viewport is setup with a custom upscaler. The main issue here is that we suppress MetalFX, so adding Custom as a enum at the end is not possible (unless there is an alternative way to fill the dropdown).\r\n\r\nImplements: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13718","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4